<urn:usf:rule:cli-inventory-classification:1> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "Require a bijection between mechanically enumerated paths and unique valid classification subjects for the selected contract. Refuse orphan, duplicate, ambiguous owner, malformed token path or stale source classifications. transition-adapter requires exact descriptor commandPath, unique command ownership, and actual admitted adapter mapping. generic-interrogation requires exact registered observation command or uniquely owned command mode, explicit no-effect semantics and compiled implementation. group-only requires actual dispatcher evidence of no default effect and complete child enumeration. non-participating requires exact graph-authored retirement or disjoint scope and rationale; an implementation label, unknown owner or lack of descriptor is never exclusion evidence. All class evidence must be independently read from actual current semantic resources, not merely nonempty basis IRIs." <urn:usf:graph:cli-inventory> .
