<urn:usf:rule:cli-inventory-required-circuit:1> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "Preserve every selected required transition and its command. Additionally protect the required Linear/Hermes circuit governed by urn:usf:contract:hermes-linear-autonomy:1 and urn:usf:acceptance:hermes-linear-autonomy: discovery, binding, dispatch, contribution, resolution, application, checking, integration, completion and Linear reconciliation. Missing graph command/transition ownership is CLI_INVENTORY_REQUIRED_CIRCUIT_UNOWNED, not non-participating. Existing hermes and linear-binding dispatch families require exact endpoint accounting including modes not exposed as registry topics. Underlying required review is not retired by retirement of the old review command shape. Explicit group roots may be group-only only when every executable descendant is accounted for. No live commissioning claim, no transfer of implementation to USF-1189." <urn:usf:graph:cli-inventory> .
